# TalentPilot AI — Cursor Rules

You are working on **TalentPilot AI**. Read and follow **[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)** for full agent guidance. First-time setup: **[SETUP.md](SETUP.md)**. Keep AGENTS.md, SETUP.md, README.md, and this file updated when conventions or setup steps change.

## Stack locks

- Backend: Python 3.11+/3.12, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy, Google Gemini, PyMuPDF, python-docx
- Frontend: Vanilla JS (ES modules) + CSS variables — **no React/Next/Vue/Angular**
- UI themes: light + dark (`data-theme`), purple/orange brand accents
- Local run: `make run`; containers: `make docker-up`

## Architecture

```text
api (thin) → application (use cases) → infrastructure (db / gemini / parser)
                ↘ domain (exceptions, enums)
middleware (request-id, security headers, rate-limit)
```

- Never put business logic in routes
- Inject via FastAPI `Depends` (`app/api/deps.py`) or constructors
- Persistence only through repositories
- LLM behind `LLMClient`; Gemini in `infrastructure/gemini/`

## Naming

- Classes / exceptions: PascalCase
- Functions / variables / modules: snake_case
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Booleans: `is_`, `has_`, `can_`

## Quality bar

- Type-hint public functions
- No `print()` — use structured logging
- No bare `except`
- Domain errors from `app.domain.exceptions`
- Validate uploads (stream size, extension, magic bytes)
- Never commit `.env`, `creds/`, or `*.db`
- Tests for every public behavior change (`make test` / `make cov`)
- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` and AGENTS.md when architecture or agent rules change

## Frontend & theme

- Structure: `frontend/js/{config,components,services,utils,pages}`
- Themes: `frontend/css/styles.css` + `utils/theme.js` + `theme-boot.js`
- Always update **both** light and dark tokens when changing UI colors
- Prefer `textContent` / `utils/dom.js` — avoid unsafe `innerHTML`
- No inline app JavaScript in HTML

## Commands

- `make run`, `make test`, `make cov`, `make docker-up`, `make docker-down`
